{"core": "Authority sets the terms — it draws the line, names what stands and what doesn't, and holds that line. In Culture, it operates on the shared rules a group already lives by: the unspoken agreements, the inherited order, the way things are done here. Overdone, Authority redraws those lines faster than the group can absorb them — the edicts keep arriving, compliance frays, and the order meant to hold things together starts to splinter from the top.", "sheetLine": "The rules keep changing before anyone has learned the last ones."}
